<!-- Bottom-nav "Settings" glyph, active/filled state.

     Geometry is character-for-character ic_nav_settings_outline.xml - same
     gear path, same 1.0 stroke. The stroke moves from fm_ink_dim to
     fm_primary and the transparent fill becomes fm_primary, so the outer
     silhouette does not move between states (it previously shrank 0.6dp on
     selection). See the Design Decisions Log in Confluence, "Selected nav
     glyphs keep their stroke" (2026-09-22), and DESIGN-SYSTEM-PHASE3.md 6.9.

     KNOWN, TRACKED SEPARATELY: this pair is still on a 24x24 viewport while
     ic_nav_groups_* and ic_nav_history_* are on 28x28. itemIconSize is 28dp,
     so this glyph is scaled 1.167x at render and its 1.0 stroke lands at
     ~1.17dp against 1.9dp and 1.8dp on its neighbours - the gear outline
     reads about a third lighter than the other two. Do NOT "fix" that by
     changing strokeWidth here alone: the two states would stop matching. It
     needs the same 24->28 viewport migration History already had.

     INVARIANT: the selected silhouette must be a strict superset of the
     unselected one - zero pixels lost at any edge. -->
